    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y=-23e\\ln x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-23e\\ln x) \\\\  & =-23e\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =-23e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{23e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "7c2ad82f-517d-5981-88e6-6b28300d4d4f",
